IMPORT prelude

-- Education Endowment and Savings Schemes Act 1992 (Singapore) -- the Post-Secondary Education (PSE) Scheme: who is a member
-- (s 20), withdrawals and who may make them (s 22), donations (s 23), transfers out and the closing of the account (s 24), who
-- authorises (s 25), and protection from creditors (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 January 2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EESSA1992.txt.
--
-- WHY. Written on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0014 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-simone, event e030: a
-- 19-year-old citizen matriculating at a local university in August 2022 pays part of her fees from her PSE account).
--
-- AGES are completed years. The Act says "attained 21 years of age" without its own rule for when an age is attained; see
-- REQ-0263.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Edusave Scheme (Parts 2 to 3), contributions and the Government's matching (s 21; the caps are prescribed),
-- interest, the "prescribed purposes" and "prescribed requirements" (regulations under s 35, not retrieved), which courses and
-- institutions the Minister has approved (an input), offences and administration.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Education Endowment and Savings Schemes Act 1992 -- the PSE Scheme`

§§ `20 -- members`

-- s 20: a person is a member of the PSE Fund "if the person -- (a) is a citizen of Singapore; and (b) satisfies any other
-- prescribed requirements".
GIVEN `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the PSE Fund` `is a citizen` `meets the prescribed requirements` IF
    `is a citizen` AND `meets the prescribed requirements`

§§ `22, 25 -- withdrawals`

-- s 22(1): money in a PSE account "may be withdrawn from that Fund with the authority of the PSE Scheme Administrator".
-- s 22(2): "a parent of a member of the PSE Fund below 21 years of age, or a member of that Fund who has attained 21 years of
-- age, is entitled to withdraw at any time the sum standing to the member's credit ... (a) to pay for all fees and charges
-- incurred or to be incurred in respect of any approved course of study or programme which is attended or to be attended by
-- the member or any sibling of the member at any approved institution; and (b) for any other prescribed purpose."
-- s 22(5): "approved" means approved by the Minister for the purposes of subsection (2).
-- s 25(1): on application by the parent or member, "the PSE Scheme Administrator may authorise the withdrawal of such sum as the
-- parent or member is entitled to withdraw".
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `the member`
    `a parent of the member`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Withdrawal request` HAS
    `member's age` IS A NUMBER
    `who applies` IS A Applicant
    `for fees of a course attended by the member or a sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `course or programme approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `institution approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for another prescribed purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `Withdrawal request`
GIVETH A Applicant
`who may withdraw` r MEANS
    IF r's `member's age` AT LEAST 21 THEN `the member` ELSE `a parent of the member`

GIVEN r IS A `Withdrawal request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is for a permitted purpose` r IF
       (    r's `for fees of a course attended by the member or a sibling`
        AND r's `course or programme approved by the Minister`
        AND r's `institution approved by the Minister`)
    OR r's `for another prescribed purpose`

GIVEN r IS A `Withdrawal request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is entitled to withdraw under section 22(2)` r IF
    r's `who applies` EQUALS `who may withdraw` r AND `is for a permitted purpose` r

GIVETH A STRING
`who authorises a withdrawal` MEANS "the PSE Scheme Administrator"

-- s 22(3), (4): on application by the member (or a parent, if the member is under 21), the Minister may permit withdrawal of
-- the WHOLE sum "if the Minister is satisfied that it is just and equitable to do so"; the account is then closed and the
-- member ceases to be a member.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, applicant IS A Applicant, `the Minister is satisfied it is just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the whole sum may be withdrawn under section 22(3)` age applicant `the Minister is satisfied it is just and equitable` IF
        `the Minister is satisfied it is just and equitable`
    AND (   applicant EQUALS `the member`
         OR (age LESS THAN 21 AND applicant EQUALS `a parent of the member`))

§§ `23 -- donation to an education charity`

-- s 23(1): the member, or a parent if the member is under 21, may donate all or part of the sum "to a prescribed charity ...
-- whose objects are exclusively or primarily for the advancement of education".
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, donor IS A Applicant, `charity prescribed, for education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may donate the PSE moneys` age donor `charity prescribed, for education` IF
        `charity prescribed, for education`
    AND (   donor EQUALS `the member`
         OR (age LESS THAN 21 AND donor EQUALS `a parent of the member`))

§§ `24 -- closing the account`

-- s 24(1): a member aged 21 or more may apply to transfer the whole sum to his or her CPF ordinary account; the account closes.
-- s 24(4): once the member reaches the prescribed "relevant age", if no application to withdraw or transfer is made within the
-- period (not exceeding 12 months) the Administrator specifies, and no extension under (3) is granted, the Administrator
-- "must transfer" the sum to the CPF ordinary account. (4A): it is then a cash grant under CPF Act s 14(1).
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to transfer the whole sum to the CPF ordinary account` age IF age AT LEAST 21

GIVEN `attained the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since then` IS A NUMBER, `period specified, in months` IS A NUMBER, `application made` IS A BOOLEAN, `extension granted under section 24(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Administrator must transfer the sum to the CPF ordinary account` `attained the relevant age` `months since then` `period specified, in months` `application made` `extension granted under section 24(3)` IF
        `attained the relevant age`
    AND `months since then` GREATER THAN `the specified period, capped at 12 months` `period specified, in months`
    AND NOT `application made`
    AND NOT `extension granted under section 24(3)`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the specified period, capped at 12 months` n MEANS IF n GREATER THAN 12 THEN 12 ELSE n

§§ `26 -- protection`

-- s 26(1): moneys in a PSE account "belong to the member and are not assignable or liable to be attached, sequestered or levied
-- upon for or in respect of any debt or claim".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `PSE moneys can be attached for the member's debts` IF FALSE
